  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">News gathering and broadcasting through FM radios to promote nation building in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Catholic Radio Network (CRN) is a media initiative with nine FM radio stations: eight in the Catholic Dioceses of the Republic of South Sudan and one in the Nuba Mountains. The Juba-based centre of coordination, administration and production of news and shared programs in English is its hub. The objectives of CRN which is aimed at being achieved in this project is to promote peaceful coexistence among ethnic groups, and to empower indigenous people, especially women and illiterate, to get more involved in decision making and take active part in the political process in the Republic of South Sudan. The project will achieve this through informing and keeping the population with relevant news items in different languages to foster political participation even among the marginalized groups, especially those who are not able to understand English and Arabic. The constitution making process, that has been temporarily halted, will continue to receive adequate coverage in the CRN radio stations, to promote people&#x2019;s participation in the process.</narrative>
  </description>
